# RediWala

RediWala is a hyperlocal platform connecting mobile street vendors with
nearby neighbourhood customers.

The initial pilot is intended for Chennai, India.

## Product Experiences

RediWala has two distinct user experiences.

### Vendor

The vendor app allows a street vendor to:

- Create and manage a profile
- Specify products, services or recyclable materials collected
- Go live while travelling through a neighbourhood
- Broadcast location only during an active session
- Receive customer interest or wait requests
- Record sales
- Record buy-back payments
- View earnings and transaction history

### Customer

The customer app allows a customer to:

- Create a private alert point
- Follow preferred vendors
- Maintain a wishlist
- Receive proximity notifications
- View a nearby vendor
- Ask a vendor to wait
- Manage alert preferences
- Review transaction history

## Application Structure

The codebase will contain:

- RediWalaVendor
- RediWalaCustomer
- Shared Swift code

Development bundle identifiers:

- com.rediwala.vendor.dev
- com.rediwala.customer.dev

Production bundle identifiers:

- com.rediwala.vendor
- com.rediwala.customer

## Proximity Model

Do not treat 500 metres as arrival.

Default alert stages:

- Nearby: approximately 500 metres
- Approaching: approximately 150 metres
- At my street: approximately 75 metres

Distances must be configurable.

The customer alert point may represent:

- Home entrance
- Apartment gate
- Street corner
- Community entrance
- Preferred meeting point

Customer alert-point coordinates are private.

