## Architecture

Use this dependency direction:

SwiftUI View
→ ViewModel
→ Repository protocol
→ Firebase or platform implementation

Rules:

- SwiftUI views contain presentation logic only.
- ViewModels are annotated with @MainActor.
- Firebase calls do not belong in views.
- Firebase calls remain inside repositories or services.
- Core Location remains inside a dedicated location provider.
- Use dependency injection.
- Use async and await.
- Do not use force unwraps.
- Do not silently ignore errors.
- Build after each small implementation task.
- Do not generate entire features in one prompt.

## Privacy

- Vendors must not receive customer alert-point coordinates.
- Customer addresses must not be exposed through follower data.
- Vendor location is published only during an active Go Live session.
- Going offline must stop location collection and invalidate presence.
- Logs must not contain phone numbers, full addresses, tokens, UPI identifiers
  or precise private coordinates.

## Environments

Use separate Firebase projects:

- rediwala-dev
- rediwala-staging
- rediwala-prod

Development builds must never use production data.

## Localization

Initial languages:

- English
- Tamil

Do not hard-code visible user-facing strings inside SwiftUI views.

## Development Approach

- Plan before generating code.
- Work in small, testable increments.
- Show proposed file changes before broad edits.
- Do not add dependencies without approval.
- Do not invent Apple or Firebase APIs.
- Use APIs supported by the installed SDK versions.